    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the roster, as his elite score of 81.88 makes him the clear foundation of the offense. Facing Bibee, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a high-park-factor environment and a favorable matchup against a pitcher with a slow delivery, which specifically incentivizes his stolen base potential\u2014the most critical variable in our 5x5 Roto construction. **Jackson Merrill** also provides immense value with a 75.27 score against the struggling Cornelio (5.59 xERA), while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** offers a strong 73.66 efficiency rating, bolstered significantly by a 17% boost from his favorable matchup against Hughes. These players are the engine for our pursuit of category gains today, leveraging high-order lineup positioning to maximize plate appearances.\n\nWhile the primary lineup is optimized for output, **Liam Hicks** (57.76) and **Drake Baldwin** (58.65) occupy the catcher slots as marginal but necessary starters given the thin depth. The most difficult decision today involved the marginal gap between these catchers and our bench assets; while we monitor prospects like **Jacob Wilson** and **Heliot Ramos**, the current lineup configuration reflects a prioritization of daily efficiency scores over speculative upside. We remain heavily constrained by the status of our elite roster anchors\u2014**Kyle Tucker**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jordan Westburg** all remain unavailable due to IL or rest, forcing us to rely on the depth of players like **Coby Mayo**, who holds a 60.78 score. Caution is advised with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.67); while his matchup against Perkins is favorable, his lineup position remains \"Pending,\" and any late-day adjustments to the batting order could see his score fluctuate. We are avoiding any unnecessary risks by keeping secondary depth pieces like **Nasim Nunez**, **Josh Jung**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, **Franklin Arias**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Tommy White** on the bench to preserve our remaining game caps for higher-leverage matchups later in the week.",
